@HD	VN:1.6	SO:unsorted
@SQ	SN:chr1	LN:40
@CO	0-based    0         1         2         3
@CO	           0123456789012345678901234567890123456789
@CO	chr1       ACGTTGCAAGGCCTTAGCATGCAATCGGATCCTAGGCTAA
@CO	Columns for each CIGAR operation, default policy (skip I) and --insertions emit. S never produces columns.
@CO	eqx: 2=2X4M at 2; bases 4,5 of the read mismatch. = and X behave exactly like M.
@CO	del_0/del_16: 4M2D4M at 5; reference 9,10 deleted. Deletion columns: read '.', off = previous base's.
@CO	ins_0/ins_16: 4M2I4M at 5; SEQ offsets 4,5 are the inserted AA.
@CO	sclip_0/sclip_16: 2S6M3S at 10; clipped GG (SEQ 0-1) and TTT (SEQ 8-10): no columns, but counted in the offsets.
@CO	lead_ins: 2I6M at 10 (insertion before the first aligned base).
@CO	hclip: 3H6M2H at 10; hard clips are not in SEQ and change nothing.
@CO	padop: 4M2P4M at 5; P changes nothing (identical to 8M).
eqx	0	chr1	3	60	2=2X4M	*	0	0	GTGTCAAG	+,-./012
del_0	0	chr1	6	60	4M2D4M	*	0	0	GCAACCTT	+,-./012
ins_0	0	chr1	6	60	4M2I4M	*	0	0	GCAAAAGGCC	+,-./01234
sclip_0	0	chr1	11	60	2S6M3S	*	0	0	GGGCCTTATTT	+,-./012345
del_16	16	chr1	6	60	4M2D4M	*	0	0	GCAACCTT	+,-./012
ins_16	16	chr1	6	60	4M2I4M	*	0	0	GCAAAAGGCC	+,-./01234
sclip_16	16	chr1	11	60	2S6M3S	*	0	0	GGGCCTTATTT	+,-./012345
lead_ins	0	chr1	11	60	2I6M	*	0	0	AAGCCTTA	+,-./012
hclip	0	chr1	11	60	3H6M2H	*	0	0	GCCTTA	+,-./0
padop	0	chr1	6	60	4M2P4M	*	0	0	GCAAGGCC	+,-./012
